# ── RE_Library : what ships is the ANALYSIS, not the corpus ──
# Sources are public at known commits; binaries are 3rd-party and large.
#
# ANCHORING NOTE — this file lives at the repo root, and the tree lives under
# RE_Library/. A .gitignore pattern containing a slash is anchored to THIS
# directory, so `07_OUTPUT/extractions/` matches nothing. Every rule below that
# names a subpath therefore carries the `RE_Library/` prefix.
#
# The previous revision of this file omitted that prefix on every slashed rule.
# It looked correct and ignored nothing except the slash-free rule at line ~9.
# Verified with `git check-ignore -v` against a live control.

# Third-party source clones (public, re-obtainable).
# Slash-free, so these match at any depth — they were the only rules that worked.
01_SOURCE_c2/
01_SOURCE_mobile/
02_BINARIES/
05_TARGETS/
03_SAMPLES/

# Scratch: extraction dumps, raw string spills, per-target work products.
RE_Library/07_OUTPUT/extractions/
extractions/

# Tooling scratch: intermediate .gem extraction layers (data.tar / data.tar.gz).
# The unpacked *source* trees (rex-socket-0.1.71/ etc.) stay tracked; only the
# throwaway stages go. Trailing slash matters: rs/ is scratch, rs3/ is not.
RE_Library/04_TOOLS/gems/rs/
RE_Library/04_TOOLS/gems/rs2/
RE_Library/04_TOOLS/gems/final/
RE_Library/04_TOOLS/gems/*.gem
RE_Library/04_TOOLS/gems/**/*.gem
RE_Library/04_TOOLS/gems/data.tar
RE_Library/04_TOOLS/gems/**/data.tar
RE_Library/04_TOOLS/gems/**/*.gz

# Same patterns without the prefix, so they hold if the tree is ever moved up.
gems/rs/
gems/rs2/
gems/final/
*.gem

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
